00:06:26.680 --> 00:06:28.660
OK, let's pop the hood on this one.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:33.120
Everyone talks about speculative decoding as a simple speed knob.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.340
In practice, it is a tight coupling between drafter size, acceptance rate, and KV cache layout

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:44.000
that only works when the drafter and target share enough cross-attention structure.

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:49.800
The D-flash approach replaces token by token speculation with a single cross-attention

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:55.860
forward pass from a smaller drafter, which is why a five-bit drafter can still propose

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:59.420
useful sequences at 30 to 51 percent acceptance.

00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:04.200
Adding KV compression on top changes the memory bandwidth trade-off.

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:12.980
Q40-Turbo-4 keeps perplexity statistically identical to the KQ8-VQ51 baseline while

00:07:12.980 --> 00:07:19.380
cutting cache traffic enough to reach 3.18 times throughput on an RTX 5,090.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:25.540
The quality gain disappears once the drafter's acceptance rate falls below about 25 percent.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:32.120
Which is why Turbo2-TCQ variants show both higher speed-up and measurable perplexity degradation.

00:07:32.780 --> 00:07:35.900
Run the compressed path on memory-bound local setups.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:42.200
Fall back to full precision KV when you need maximum acceptance on long-context agent traces.

00:07:42.960 --> 00:07:49.540
The gacha that bites most teams is assuming the drafter and target quantizations can be chosen independently.

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.580
Mis-matched layouts destroy the cross-attention benefit.

00:07:54.140 --> 00:08:02.640
Run the Q40-Turbo-4D flash configuration on twin 3.627b if you need faster local coding agents

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:09.000
without measurable quality loss. Test Medi's PII on your own synthetic clinical notes

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:14.300
to see how well it preserves lab values and medication timelines while stripping identifiers.

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:23.120
Point VLLM doctor at any production VLLM endpoint to surface KV cache pressure before it causes timeouts.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:34.280
Compare Google's Gemma 4 QAT-Q4-0GGUF against unslots the UD-Q4K-XL on the same E4B checkpoint

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:37.860
to measure the effect of the extra projection tensors.

